# Service Name Mappings (Docker Compose vs Kubernetes)
#
# This file serves as documentation for how service names translate
# between your local Docker Compose environment and your Minikube cluster.

# --- WAF Service ---
# Docker Compose: postgres://postgres:...@waf-db:5432/waf_logs
# Kubernetes:     postgres://$(WAF_DB_USER):$(WAF_DB_PASSWORD)@waf-db-cluster-rw:5432/waf_logs
# Reason: K8s uses CloudNativePG which creates a read-write service named `<cluster-name>-rw`

# --- WAF Redis ---
# Docker Compose: redis://waf-redis:6379
# Kubernetes:     redis://waf-redis-ha-master:6379
# Reason: K8s uses a Redis High Availability Helm chart which suffixes the master node

# --- Proxy Service ---
# VOTE_SERVICE_URI=http://vote:80
# RESULT_SERVICE_URI=http://result:80
# Note: These names are UNIFORM. Both Docker Compose and Kubernetes use 'vote' and 'result'
# as the service names, so the proxy configuration is identical in both environments.

# --- Result App ---
# Docker Compose: POSTGRES_HOST=db
# Kubernetes:     POSTGRES_HOST=db-cluster-rw
# Reason: CloudNativePG manages the Postgres database in K8s.
